# AgentSec UI Design System

Canonical tokens: `docs/AGENTSEC_DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`. Review: `.cursor/skills/ui-review/SKILL.md`.

Learner-facing surfaces (AcmeBank, Attack Service, Studio workshops) share one palette. Do not restyle Splunk login or enterprise chrome.

## Tokens

Background: #F6F8FB
Panel: #FFFFFF
Primary text: #17202A
Secondary text: #3D4654 (AA on page). Do not use #5B6573 for captions.
Primary navy: #0B1F33
Accent teal: #007F86
Success: #2E7D32
Warning: #B7791F
Critical: #C62828
Information: #3568A8
Advanced/ML: #6B46C1 (MLTK track only)
Borders: #D9E0E7

Focus: 2px solid #007F86, 2px offset.
Primary buttons ≥44px tall. Body ≥16px equivalent.

## Rules

- Severity is never color alone (ALLOW, DENY, SIMULATED, LIVE, BASELINE, ATTACK, RETEST).
- Empty tables stay visible; explain zero rows.
- Splunk UI copy must not imply the dashboard DENYs the loan.
- Studio: GRID, 12-column, tabs for workshop steps.
- No neon, no extra charts, no MLTK purple on first lab.
